    "body": "## Summary\n- `reasonAboutBlock` (block-reason.ts) splits the GENUINE BLOCKER bucket in two: a new\n  `fixable_blocker` disposition for a block whose evidence is a red required check\n  (`blocked_ci`) or a `blocked_review` with a nameable unmet criterion (an optional\n  `BlockEvidence.unmetCriteria` param) -- the SAME two signals sweep.ts's `isBlockedCi` /\n  `unmetCriteria.length > 0` rows read for its `blocked-fixable` disposition (W1-T77),\n  mirrored rather than re-derived. Anything else stays `genuine_blocker` -- halt narrows to\n  that truly-stuck case, it is not removed.\n- `runDaemon` (daemon.ts) gains an optional `dispatchFixRung` hook, tried BEFORE halting on a\n  `fixable_blocker`. `\"fixed\"` flags the task (`next.status = \"blocked\"`, so `runOne` never\n  re-runs it this boot -- the dispatched fix rides the task's existing open PR forward via\n  `deps.sweep`'s own per-tick reconciliation, never a second parallel run) and the drain keeps\n  going. `\"escalate\"` (or the hook simply not being wired) falls through to the exact same\n  halt+escalate path a non-fixable genuine blocker takes -- a strike-exhausted/refused fix\n  attempt still escalates for re-judgment, it never fix-loops forever (the W1-T168\n  anti-regression this ticket is explicitly the sibling of).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. \"a FIXABLE genuine blocker is delegated to the fix rung ... not halted-and-escalated\"\n   Proven by unit tests over `reasonAboutBlock`'s genuine-blocker branch in\n   `test/block-reason.test.ts`:\n   - `reasonAboutBlock: the #383/DAEMON-1784570007163 FALSIFIER -- a blocked_ci strike on B\n     (C transitively needs it) is FIXABLE, not a truly-stuck genuine blocker` -- reproduces the\n     exact real-world fixture (a `blocked_ci` block with a real dependent) and asserts\n     `{ kind: \"fixable_blocker\", dependents: [\"C\"] }`, i.e. it no longer falls into the\n     halt-triggering `genuine_blocker` bucket.\n   - `reasonAboutBlock: a blocked_review strike WITH a nameable unmet criterion (evidence) is\n     also FIXABLE` -- proves the review-side signal routes to `fixable_blocker` too.\n   On the daemon/caller side, `test/daemon.test.ts`'s\n   `W1-T174 FIXABLE BLOCKER: dispatchFixRung 'fixed' skips the halt -- B is flagged (never\n   re-run), unrelated D still drains, C stays gated on B` proves `runDaemon` never reaches\n   `daemon.blocked`/`escalateBlock` for this case, and instead calls `dispatchFixRung` exactly\n   once and keeps draining.\n   Run: `node --test --import tsx --import ./test/setup/tmp-hygiene.ts test/block-reason.test.ts test/daemon.test.ts`\n   (grep the output for `FALSIFIER` / `FIXABLE BLOCKER` -- all pass).\n\n2. \"an UNFIXABLE / ambiguous genuine blocker still halts + escalates ... halt narrows to the\n   truly-stuck ... must NOT regress into W1-T168's class\"\n   Proven by:\n   - `reasonAboutBlock: a blocked_review strike with NO nameable unmet criterion stays a\n     genuine (truly-stuck) blocker` (block-reason.test.ts) -- asserts the pre-existing\n     `{ kind: \"genuine_blocker\", dependents: [\"C\"] }` shape is unchanged with no evidence.\n   - The two PRE-EXISTING tests `reasonAboutBlock: a strike on B ...` / `... on A ...` still\n     pass byte-for-byte unmodified (same `genuine_blocker` shape), proving no regression for\n     callers with no fixable signal.\n   - `test/daemon.test.ts`'s `W1-T174 FIX RUNG ESCALATE: dispatchFixRung reporting 'escalate'\n     falls through to the SAME halt+escalate a truly-stuck blocker takes (W1-T168\n     anti-regression -- never fix-loop forever)` -- a strike-exhausted fix attempt still halts\n     + escalates exactly once, never retries the rung itself.\n   - `W1-T174 opt-in only: with NO dispatchFixRung hook wired, a FIXABLE (blocked_ci) blocker\n     still halts+escalates exactly as before this hook existed` -- proves the pre-existing\n     `stop-on-block`/`W1-T46 GENUINE BLOCKER` tests' behavior is preserved when the new hook\n     isn't wired.\n   Run: same command as above -- all new + pre-existing genuine-blocker/stop-on-block tests\n   pass (98/98 across the two files combined).\n\n## Verification\n- `npm run build` (tsc, no errors).\n- `node --test --import tsx --import ./test/setup/tmp-hygiene.ts test/block-reason.test.ts test/daemon.test.ts`\n  -- 12/12 and 86/86 pass (7 new tests: 4 in block-reason.test.ts, 3 in daemon.test.ts; all\n  pre-existing tests in both files pass unmodified).\n- Full `npm test` run: 243 pre-existing failures, all in `serve*.test.ts`/panel routes\n  (confirmed via `git stash` on the same tree -- identical failures with none of this diff\n  applied), none touching `block-reason`, `daemon`, `sweep`, or `run-task`.\n\nRemudero-Task: W1-T174\n",
